# Analytic pieces and measurable rigidity

Formalization of the section "Analytic pieces and measurable rigidity" of the blueprint
(labels `rig:common-core`, `rig:translation-matrices`, `rig:pieces`, `rig:analytic-rigidity`,
`rig:exact`).

## Design choices

* The base translate `E_h = {(x,θ) : (x+h,θ) ∈ E}` is `Auto.baseShift h E`, with vertex sets
  `X_j - h = Auto.aux_vertexShift h X j`.
* The cores `(F_h; Y_{j,h})` of `rig:common-core` are given as functions of `h`, so that the
  convergence `|X_j \ Y_{j,h}| → 0` can be stated; the properties for a single `h` are bundled
  in `Auto.aux_IsCommonCore`.
* The rows `Φ_j(z) = (φ^1_j(z), …, φ^d_j(z))` of an orthonormal basis of `K_E` are
  `Auto.basisRow b j z : Fin d → ℝ`; right multiplication of a row by a matrix is
  `Matrix.vecMul`.
* "Real analytic on all of `ℝ²`" is `AnalyticOnNhd ℝ g univ`; `Mᵀ` is
  `ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint (M α β)`.
-/

